---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Contact ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: a rule, a question, the widget`} description="Write to State Permit Test when a state rule looks out of date, when a practice question seems wrong, or to embed the free permit practice test on a school or library website." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Contact' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. A person reads every message.</p>
    <h2>A state rule looks out of date</h2>
    <p>Tell us the state, the rule and, if you have it, the page of the state agency or the handbook edition that says otherwise. Legislatures change permit ages, hours and fees, and some agencies update their web pages before their handbook. We read the official page again, correct the data file and date the change.</p>
    <h2>A practice question seems wrong</h2>
    <p>Give us the first words of the question. Each question names the handbook chapter or federal rule it was written from; if the rule differs in your state, we say so in the explanation or remove the question from that state's test.</p>
    <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
    <p>We are not a DMV. We cannot book a test, check a permit, change a record or answer for a state agency. Please do not send your license number, date of birth or address.</p>
    <h2>Using the test on your own site</h2>
    <p>Driving schools, high schools, libraries and community centers can show the practice test in an iframe at no cost. The code and conditions are on the <a href={route('widget', lang)}>embed page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
